Package: holyphp
Version: 1.0.0
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: HolyPHP <holyphp@localhost>
Installed-Size: 4096
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.17)
Recommends: gcc
Suggests: build-essential
Homepage: https://localhost/holyphp
Description: compiled, memory-safe programming language with the soul of PHP
 HolyPHP compiles .hphp source to native machine code through its own C
 backend: PHP-flavored syntax ($variables, echo, foreach), a compile-time
 borrow checker, ownership (own<T>), and raw pointers only inside unsafe.
 .
 The package contains the self-contained `hphp` compiler (runtime and
 standard library embedded). It installs /usr/bin/hphp so `hphp run`,
 `hphp build` and `hphp pkg` work immediately in any shell.
 .
 Libraries such as ui and websocket are NOT included; install them with
 the built-in package manager: `hphp install ui`.
